Add EUPL-1.1 and EUPL-1.2 to the SPDX licence allow-list.

nextcloud/openapi-extractor maps an app's <licence> to an SPDX identifier
through a hardcoded match() in src/Helpers.php, and calls Logger::panic()
— a fatal — on anything it does not recognise. EUPL-1.2 is a valid SPDX
identifier (https://spdx.org/licenses/EUPL-1.2.html) and is the licence
every Conduction Nextcloud app ships under, so the tool cannot run against
any of them:

  PHP Fatal error: license: Unable to convert EUPL-1.2 to SPDX identifier

EUPL-1.1 is included for the same reason — it is equally valid SPDX and
would fail identically.

Upstream: https://github.com/nextcloud/openapi-extractor
Checked against upstream main on 2026-08-18: still missing.

--- a/src/Helpers.php
+++ b/src/Helpers.php
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
 			'mpl' => 'MPL-2.0',
 			'apache' => 'Apache-2.0',
 			'gpl3' => 'GPL-3.0-only',
-			'AGPL-3.0-only', 'AGPL-3.0-or-later', 'Apache-2.0', 'GPL-3.0-only', 'GPL-3.0-or-later', 'MIT', 'MPL-2.0' => $license,
+			'AGPL-3.0-only', 'AGPL-3.0-or-later', 'Apache-2.0', 'EUPL-1.1', 'EUPL-1.2', 'GPL-3.0-only', 'GPL-3.0-or-later', 'MIT', 'MPL-2.0' => $license,
 			default => Logger::panic('license', 'Unable to convert ' . $license . ' to SPDX identifier'),
 		};
 
